Subject: [PATCH 324/488] soh: name the 10 address-named symbols defined in
 z_en_horse_ganon.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 10 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Horse_Ganon/z_en_horse_ganon.c.

  * D_80A69248 -> sPathPoints
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the fourteen waypoints the phantom horse
    gallops between, each carrying an XYZ position and the speed to hold on
    the way to it.

  * D_80A692B8 -> sHoofstepFrames
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the two animation frames at which the walking
    hoofstep sfx fires, stepped through by soundCount.

  * func_80A68660 -> EnHorseGanon_GetPathPoint
    deduced, confidence HIGH: copies one sPathPoints entry's position into a
    Vec3f.

  * func_80A686A8 -> EnHorseGanon_FollowPath
    deduced, confidence HIGH: advances to the next waypoint once within 400
    units, turns toward it at a capped rate, and holds that waypoint's speed
    except when the player is close, where it sprints instead.

  * func_80A68870 -> EnHorseGanon_PlayWalkSfx
    deduced, confidence HIGH: fires the walking hoofstep sfx as the
    animation passes each of sHoofstepFrames.

  * func_80A68AC4 -> EnHorseGanon_SetupIdle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs action 0 and loops the idle
    animation.

  * func_80A68AF0 -> EnHorseGanon_Idle
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sActionFuncs[0]: keeps the horse stopped and
    just advances its animation.

  * func_80A68B20 -> EnHorseGanon_SetupGallop
    deduced, confidence HIGH: installs action 1 and picks the walk, trot or
    gallop animation from the current speed, scaling its playback rate to
    match and playing the running sfx for the faster two.

  * func_80A68DB0 -> EnHorseGanon_Gallop
    deduced, confidence HIGH: sActionFuncs[1]: plays the hoofsteps for the
    walk animation, follows the path, and re-picks the gait each time the
    animation loops round.

  * func_80A68E14 -> EnHorseGanon_PitchToSlope
    deduced, confidence HIGH: raycasts for the floor 30 units ahead and
    pitches the horse to match the slope it is about to run onto.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
